wajo25_q4.solution:
Solution. Answer: 52. Let $\overline{a b}$ be the decimal digit representation of Anna's current age.<br>Then<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
\overline{b a}+1 &amp; =\frac{1}{2} \cdot \overline{a b} \\
\text { i.e. } 10 b+a+1 &amp; =\frac{1}{2}(10 a+b) \\
20 b+2 a+2 &amp; =10 a+b \\
19 b &amp; =8 a-2
\end{aligned}
$$<br>Since RHS(*) is even, $b$ is even.<br>Also, $a$ is a leading digit which implies<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
&amp; 1 \leqslant a \quad \leqslant 9 \\
\Longrightarrow &amp; 6 \leqslant 8 a-2 \leqslant 70 \\
\Longrightarrow &amp; 0&lt;b \quad&lt;4 \\
\Longrightarrow &amp; b=2, \quad \text { is the only possibility, since } b \text { is even. }
\end{aligned}
$$<br>Checking with $b=2$, we have $a=5$; i.e. $b=2$ works.<br>Hence Anna's age $\overline{a b}=52$.<br><b>Alternatively,</b> after ( * ) above, and observing $b$ is even, we make $a$ the subject:<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
8 a &amp; =19 b+2 \\
a &amp; =\frac{1}{8}(19 b+2)
\end{aligned}
$$<br>And try cases for $b$ :<br><br>$b=0 \implies a = 2/8$<br>$b=2 \implies a = 40/8 = 5$<br>$b=4 \implies a = 78/8$<br>$b=6 \implies a = 116/8$<br>$b=8 \implies a = 148/8$<br><br>Only $b=2$ leads to $a$ being an integer, namely $a=5$.<br>So Anna's age $\overline{a b}=52$.

