Solution. Answer: 14. It's easiest to compare the numbers as $5^{\text {th }}$ powers:<br>$$
\begin{array}{rlrl}
\left(2^{02}\right)^{5}&lt; &amp; 2^{025}&lt;202^{5}&lt; &amp; \left(20^{2}\right)^{5} \\
=4^{5} &amp; &amp; =2^{5 \cdot 5} &amp; &amp; \\
&amp; &amp; =\left(2^{5}\right)^{5} &amp; &amp; =400^{5} \\
&amp; &amp; =32^{5} &amp; &amp; 
\end{array}
$$<br>So $\left(20^{2}\right)^{5}$ is the largest. Now observe that:<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
\left(20^{2}\right)^{5} &amp; =20^{10} \\
&amp; =(2 \cdot 10)^{10} \\
&amp; =2^{10} \cdot 10^{10} \\
&amp; =1024 \cdot 10^{10}
\end{aligned}
$$<br>the 4-digit number 1024 followed by 10 zeros, i.e. a 14-digit number.

wajo25_q16.solution:
Solution. Answer: 447. First observe that each of $5^{j}, 7^{\ell}, 11^{m}, 19$ and 2025 is odd.<br>So $6^{k}$ must also be odd, which since 6 is even, only occurs if $k=0$.<br>So our problem reduces to finding non-negative integers $j, \ell, m$ such that:<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
5^{j}+7^{\ell}+11^{m} &amp; =2025-19-6^{0} \\
&amp; =2005
\end{aligned}
$$<br>Observe that $5^{5}=5 \cdot 625&gt;2005$, and $11^{4}&gt;7^{4}=7 \cdot 343&gt;2005$. So $j \leqslant 4$ and $\ell, m \leqslant 3$. Now reducing (*) modulo 5, we get<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
2005 \equiv 0 &amp; \equiv 5^{j}+7^{\ell}+11^{m} \quad(\bmod 5) \\
&amp; \equiv 0+2^{\ell}+1 \quad(\bmod 5)
\end{aligned}
$$<br>The only $\ell \in\{0,1,2,3\}$ such that $2^{\ell}+1$ is a multiple of 5 , is $\ell=2$, and so our problem is now reduced to finding $j, m$ such that:<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
5^{j}+11^{m} &amp; =2005-7^{2} \\
&amp; =1956
\end{aligned}
$$<br>Now reducing (**) modulo 11, we get<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
1956 \equiv 6-5+9-1 \equiv 9 &amp; \equiv 5^{j}+11^{m} \quad(\bmod 11) \\
&amp; \equiv 5^{j} \quad(\bmod 11)
\end{aligned}
$$<br>and $5^{j} \bmod 11$ for $j=0,1,2,3,4$ gives $1,5,3,4,9$, respectively.<br>So $j=4$ giving<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
11^{m} &amp; =1956-5^{4} \\
&amp; =1331 \\
&amp; =11^{3}
\end{aligned}
$$<br>So uniquely we have $j=4, k=0, \ell=2, m=3$ and hence<br>$$
\begin{aligned}
\overline{j k \ell m} / 9 &amp; =4023 / 9 \\
&amp; =447 .
\end{aligned}
$$
